      "side": 0,
      "message": "HttpServletRequestWrapper itself does still exist — it\u0027s part of the servlet API, not Jetty. The reason this changed is that the old code did super(new Request(null, null)), and Jetty 12\u0027s org.eclipse.jetty.server.Request became an interface (no longer a concrete class), so that constructor call no longer compiles.\n\nRather than figure out a new Jetty-12 way to fabricate an empty Request, the test now extends Gerrit\u0027s own version-agnostic test fixture com.google.gerrit.util.http.testutil.FakeHttpServletRequest.\n\nThis is covered in the commit message under \"Test adaptation for Jetty 12\".",
